DO NOT LISTEN TO THE NEGATIVE REVIEWS. MOST OF THESE PEOPLE HAVEN'T TRULY PLAYED THE GAME, AND DON'T HAVE A REALISTIC VIEW OF IT.
Though it may not seem like it, I've played this game for about 4 or 5 months now. The second it hit Steam, I went ahead and re-installed so I can track my hours and whatnot. I'm level 30, and I've dabbled in the 1v1 ranked play. I have 2 diamond mages, and a handful of other gods I'm rather decent with. I won't say I'm the best player out there, but I have a fair and solid opinion of the game which I believe will be helpful to people making their judgments before downloading.
If you liked the idea of MOBA's or even enjoy other games of this genre, but you may or may not know how to feel about the top-down perspective, and the lack of immersion and precesion it brings, this is the game for you.
Smite is a truly innovative game in this genre, as it features a 3rd person (over the shoulder) perspective, and instead of using fictitious characters, it uses gods of various mythologies. (Including: Mayan, Hindu, Chinese, Roman, Greek, and Norse) And for the most part, they add a new god every month or so. The style it uses, allows you to be more hands on in the combat portion of the game, and allow for a more immersive, action-driven experience. Don't let that fool you into thinking the game is inherently "easier" than others of the genre. While it is more friendly to newer players, there is still a very strong degree of strategy that goes into this game. You use items, and actives, as well as your skill building to maximize certain assets of the characters. You have to communicate with your team, either by using the built in vgs system (a system that uses letter codes to emote certain commands, and information to your team) or by using Curse Voice and a microphone, to strategize and adapt to the situations. As well as needing to have a general knowledge of a good team makeup (Generally ADC [assassin or hunter], tank [guardian or warrior] and mage).
The game is also unique in that, unlike most other moba's, Smite has a variety of modes to try from.
- 5v5,  no lanes, straight fighting, and allowing minions to pass across the arena into the enemies base;
- 5v5, 1 lane, random gods, no returning to base;
- 3v3, 1 lane with side jungles, though otherwise typical objective based play;
- 4v4. 2 lanes, middle jungle, push siege monsters to the enemy base;
- Traditional 5v5, 3 lanes, jungles in between. As well as a special MOTD (Mode of the Day) which can be anything.
All in all, this game provides a good, unique, strategic, action-packed experience for both experienced and newer players. You start off with a decent range of gods for free, plus those included in the weekly rotation, and the rest can either be purchased in bulk with cash, or one by one with in-game currency. It is a great, rewarding free-to-play game, definitely worth giving a shot, if not making its way into your frequented games.
That is pretty much it. My in-game name is BaconBeats, I run a clan. Feel free to message or add me for questions, Joust, or if you're looking for a clan. gg

