Half Life really put other games I've played into perspective. I've always had my hand held, always had a little floating marker telling me, "Go here, push this, kill that." I've always been showered in health, just so I don't go crying to mommy because I was't taking cover. But not in half life. The puzzles are tough and not thoroughly explained, so I found myslef checking the walkthrough often (FYI, I am stupid). I still found it fun, and the platforming wan't overly impossible. What I liked most about HL was the combat. In CoD or some other modern shooter, you crouch behind a wall for 5 seconds and your bullet holes magicaly heal themselves. In Half Life, you can get knocked down to 2 health with no medkits nearby. It is then that the stakes are raised higher than any spunk-gargle weewee shooter(From
). You have to fight your way to a medkit while avoiding any kind of damage, since a tiny papercut to your pinky will kill you. Then when you finaly get said medkit, it gives a sense of accomplishment that you can never get from gunning down countless foriengers from behind a brown chest-high wall.
Overall, a very fun game and a good representation of how games have changed.
